WEBVTT
Kind: subtitles
Language: en

NOTE
English subtitles for "The UAE Through History" (IRTH). Translated from the on-screen Arabic text. Source: the Ministry of Education textbooks "The UAE: Our History".

1
00:00:20.042 --> 00:00:22.492
A journey through history
From Jebel Faya to the founding of the Union

2
00:00:22.902 --> 00:00:25.855
130,000 years ago — Jebel Faya
Stone tools reveal the arrival of some of the first humans to come out of Africa.

3
00:00:26.205 --> 00:00:31.079
8000–4000 BC — Marawah and Dalma: the Neolithic
The earliest island villages, pearl diving, and Mesopotamian pottery marking the dawn of seaborne trade.

4
00:00:31.429 --> 00:00:35.041
3000 BC — Hili: the first farms
The Hili 8 tower in Al Ain holds the earliest evidence of crop farming in the Emirates.

5
00:00:35.391 --> 00:00:39.099
3000–2500 BC — The Jebel Hafit tombs
Stone tombs on the slopes of Hafit, and the first copper tools as the Bronze Age begins.

6
00:00:39.449 --> 00:00:43.414
2500–2000 BC — The Umm an-Nar civilisation
Circular tombs and far-reaching trade; Mesopotamian texts called the land "Magan", the land of copper.

7
00:00:43.764 --> 00:00:47.278
2000–1600 BC — The Wadi Suq period
A changing climate and way of life; the tombs of Jebel Buhais preserve the jewellery of the age.

8
00:00:47.628 --> 00:00:51.561
1000 BC — The Iron Age: the aflaj
Falaj channels water the oases of Al Ain, the camel enters daily life, and fortified villages such as Muweilah rise.

9
00:00:51.911 --> 00:00:54.998
250 BC — Mleiha
A trading town in Sharjah that minted its own coins and traded as far as Petra.

10
00:00:55.348 --> 00:00:58.336
100 AD — ed-Dur
A thriving port in Umm Al Quwain, home to the first temple discovered in the Emirates.

11
00:00:58.686 --> 00:01:02.362
Before Islam — The Sir Bani Yas monastery
An ancient monastery that stood for more than a century after Islam spread — a witness to tolerance.

12
00:01:02.712 --> 00:01:06.899
632–633 AD — The dawn of Islam and the Battle of Dibba
Islam reached the Emirates in 632 and its people soon embraced it; the Battle of Dibba followed in 633.

13
00:01:07.249 --> 00:01:10.796
8th–9th century AD — The oldest mosque in the Emirates
A mud-brick mosque in Al Ain, dating roughly to the Abbasid era.

14
00:01:11.146 --> 00:01:14.660
c. 1421 — Julfar and Ibn Majid
The port of Julfar thrives on trade and pearls; the navigator Ahmad ibn Majid is born there.

15
00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:19.197
1507 — The Portuguese on the east coast
The Portuguese seized Khor Fakkan and the east coast; Julfar was freed from them around 1632.

16
00:01:19.547 --> 00:01:24.173
1761 — From Liwa to Abu Dhabi
The Bani Yas find fresh water on Abu Dhabi island; in 1795 the seat of rule moved there, and a fort rose that became the core of Qasr Al Hosn.

17
00:01:24.523 --> 00:01:28.134
18th century — The Qawasim
Sheikh Rahma bin Matar Al Qasimi founded the Qawasim emirate, which became a leading sea power in the north.

18
00:01:28.484 --> 00:01:32.608
1820 — The General Treaty of Peace
The 1820 treaty was followed by those of 1853 and 1892, and the region became known as the Trucial States.

19
00:01:32.958 --> 00:01:35.912
1833 — Al Maktoum in Dubai
The Al Maktoum settled in Dubai, and its trade flourished around the creek.

20
00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:39.547
1855–1909 — Sheikh Zayed the First
The longest reign in Abu Dhabi's history, extending its influence across a vast area.

21
00:01:39.897 --> 00:01:43.444
The 1930s — The collapse of the pearl trade
The Great Depression and cultured pearls strike the coast's main source of livelihood.

22
00:01:43.794 --> 00:01:47.178
1952 — The Trucial States Council
A council bringing the rulers together is founded, and Fujairah is recognised as an emirate in its own right.

23
00:01:47.528 --> 00:01:50.681
1958–1962 — Oil
Oil is discovered in Abu Dhabi in 1958, and the first cargo is exported in 1962.

24
00:01:51.031 --> 00:01:54.447
6 August 1966 — Zayed becomes Ruler of Abu Dhabi
Sheikh Zayed bin Sultan Al Nahyan takes office, and an era of building begins.

25
00:01:54.797 --> 00:01:59.299
18 February 1968 — The Argoub Al Sedirah meeting
After Britain announced its withdrawal, Sheikh Zayed and Sheikh Rashid agreed to unite and invited the other emirates to join.

26
00:01:59.649 --> 00:02:04.181
November 1971 — The three islands and the first martyr
Iran occupied Greater Tunb, Lesser Tunb and Abu Musa; Salem Suhail bin Khamis became the UAE's first martyr.

27
00:02:04.531 --> 00:02:07.850
2 December 1971 — The founding of the United Arab Emirates
The rulers met in Dubai and declared the Union.

28
00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:10.952
10 February 1972 — The Union is complete
Ras Al Khaimah joins, completing the seven emirates.

29
00:02:11.902 --> 00:02:15.102
The United Arab Emirates
Seven emirates • One history • One Union

